<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus's August CPI drops 1.31 pct mnth/mnth.</title>
<headline>Cyprus's August CPI drops 1.31 pct mnth/mnth.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cyprus's CPI fell by 1.31 percent in August to 114.84 points compared to 116.36 in July, the island's statistics and research department said.</p>
<p>    Consumer price index   August 96  July 96   August 95</p>
<p>    Month/month change(pct)  -1.31     0.32	 -1.59</p>
<p>    Year/year change (pct)    3.32     3.02	  2.73</p>
<p>    Index (1992 = 100)	114.84     116.36     111.14</p>
<p>The department said the fall was due to sale discounts in clothing, footwear and furniture and a decrease in the price of electricity. Increases were recorded in the prices of certain fresh fruits and vegetables.</p>
<p>-- Michele Kambas, Nicosia newsroom 357 2 365089</p>
